cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Q2D — Query-to-Data"
message: >-
  If you reference Q2D, please cite the technical report rather than this
  repository. Cite a specific draft: the protocol is pre-release and its
  claims are version-sensitive.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Oram
    given-names: Peter
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0005-0608-9792"
repository-code: "https://github.com/q2d-protocol/q2d"
url: "https://q2d.dev"
abstract: >-
  A transport-neutral protocol for policy-bound, least-disclosure answers over
  data held by a participating custodian. A requester submits a signed, typed
  answer contract binding the question, purpose, recipient, permitted sinks,
  and maximum response domain before evaluation. The custodian evaluates the
  query locally under applicable policy and returns a bounded, authenticated
  answer with a disclosure receipt.
keywords:
  - AI agents
  - data minimization
  - privacy engineering
  - policy enforcement
  - prompt injection
  - information-flow control
  - MCP
  - A2A
  - selective disclosure
  - authenticated computation
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.0.1

